WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.150
Rwanda.

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.750
In the lower house of its parliament,
women hold 63.8 per cent of the seats.

3
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.590
Yet the NGO Freedom House
rates Rwanda Not Free,

4
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.690
with a score of 21 out of 100.

5
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:18.010
Two numbers, and two very different
pictures of the same country.

6
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.990
So has human rights
governance there succeeded?

7
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.430
Do the seats prove it?

8
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.250
Does the low score cancel everything else?

9
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.150
In this mission, you'll choose
indicators for judging an intervention,

10
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.790
from health and education
to free speech and GDP.

11
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.230
Then you'll build a scorecard for Rwanda,

12
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.210
from its laws to its health
data, and weigh up the evidence.

13
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:44.040
Your mission: evaluate whether human
rights governance in Rwanda has succeeded.
